{
  "about": "The creative vocabulary of directions.py: independent axes (transitions, camera, type, colour, rhythm) whose options are built only from catalogue ids (transitions of project.ts, fonts of fonts.json, text effects of Fx.tsx, grades of grades.json). A direction is one option per axis, narrowed by the concept's restraint, so the space is large and coherent instead of a short list rotated by index. `feel` places an option on four dimensions from -1 to 1: energy (calm .. driving), warmth (cool .. warm), formality (playful .. formal), grit (clean .. rough). `selftest.sh` checks every id here against the catalogue.",
